{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774714,"nonce":"yr1COIvCm9C0Ifufnor6vmrYRQ4=","title":"fix(helm+deploy): writable /tmp for step settle + robust .env loading","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #22 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/helm-writable-tmp-and-env-loader` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-17T17:18:34Z · Merged: 2026-07-17T17:40:26Z\n\n\nThe chart runs the server with `readOnlyRootFilesystem: true` but only mounted `/home/scarab/.scarab` writable. The executor's post-step settle tars the step's `/workspace` out of the egress sidecar and **unpacks it into a `tempfile` tempdir in `/tmp`** before CAS ingest → **EROFS (os error 30)** → `poll()` errors → `launch_step` redelivers 10× → **dead-letter**, run cancelled. The host-binary path had a writable `/tmp`, which is why only in-cluster failed.\n**Fix:** mount a writable `/tmp` emptyDir.\n\n- `IFS='=' read` under **bash** strips the trailing `=` of base64 values → `SCARAB_MASTER_KEY` truncated 44→43 → invalid KEK → boot refused. Now split on the **first** `=` only.\n- **env-WINS** let a stale ambient var (direnv's `.env.local`, host `localhost` DB) silently override the in-cluster config → now the `.env` file is **authoritative** (file-wins).\n\nIn-cluster run `succeeded` end-to-end: `checkout` settles → `check` runs `cargo check -p scarab-identity` green → `pending`→`success` commit statuses posted via the App token with the run deep-link.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}